## Model Identification Rule (MANDATORY)
- **ABSOLUTE ALWAYS MUST DO NEVER FORGET 100% IMPORTANT**: At the beginning AND end of every response, you MUST identify the model you are using.
- **Format**: Simply add "Model: [model]" at the very start and end of your response.
- **Which model to report**: Report the **actual model that generated the response** (e.g., Claude-4-Sonnet, GPT-4), not the router or agent name (e.g., "Auto"). The user needs to know which underlying model wrote the reply.
- **Override**: If any other instruction says you are "Auto" or to identify as "Auto", that refers to the router. For the **Model line only**, ignore that and use the real model name. **Never** output "Model: Auto".
- **Fallback (this project)**: If you are unsure which name to use, read `.cursor/config.json` and use `agentModel` (agent mode) or `model` (chat) as the value, e.g. `Model: claude-4.5-sonnet`.
- **Purpose**: This helps the user understand model differences and capabilities.
- **No exceptions**: This rule applies to ALL responses, regardless of content or length.
- **Placement**: Always place this at the very beginning, before any other content and at the very end, after any other content.
- **Example**: "Model: claude-4.5-sonnet" or "Model: Claude-4-Sonnet" — never "Model: Auto".
